* Mirror the real 811 descendant model: `UPDATE`, `UPDATE_REMARK`, `NO_RESPONSE`, `SECOND_NOTICE`, `CORRECTION`, `RECALL` all get **new ticket numbers** but carry an `originalTicketNumber` (or `parentTicketNumber`) field. This is the same Phase 0 linkage rule we've been deferring — the simulator must emit the parent linkage so Backend ingestion and mobile history tabs can resolve ticket families without inventing their own heuristic (shared address is already flagged as a temporary hack in Phase 3).
